{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And as for you and your servants, etc.</b> He mentioned the servants, because he saw that they had not set their hearts to the word of HaShem and had left their servants and their livestock in the field — he included them together. And if you would say, who revealed to Moses that after the plague of hail they were still in their rebellion and had not been humbled? For did they not justify the judgment upon themselves afterward and say, ״HaShem is righteous, and I and my people are the wicked״? I have already written to you that HaShem made him understand that he would bring the plague of the firstborn upon the Egyptians; also according to what I explained in the verse (Exodus 7:4) ״ולא ישמע אליכם פרעה״ — that a time would arrive when he would no longer want to hear even a mission from them. If so, from this Moses knew that even when the rain, etc., would cease, they would not send the people, and he said to them, ״I know,״ etc. It will further be explained below, for there is a reason why he said from it ״טרם תיראון״." "<b>I know that before you fear.</b> Meaning: I know that before the plague is removed you fear HaShem and say, ״HaShem is righteous,״ etc., but after the plague ends and you see relief you will again rebel as at first. And you have already conducted yourself thus with me — that you agree to send the people before the plague ends, and after it ends you harden your heart." "It further intends to inform him that he knows their words are not cunning and contrivance in order that Moses would be willing to pray on their behalf, but rather their heart trembled and their spirit was terrified of HaShem Elohim — and in this there is a declaration to them that he knows a man's thoughts and his contrivances, and this matter Pharaoh will grasp by himself, for righteousness is at Moses' right hand. He also informed him hereby that he knows this is only before the plague ends, not after, when he sees relief he will rebel — and this too he will know at the end, that even when he strives to deny his prophecy and to send Israel, he will not master his spirit. Understand:"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:16.756516621Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}